If $\operatorname{char}\kappa\ne\ell$, then $$\ker\left(E^\times/E^{\times\ell}
       \xrightarrow{(\mathop{\mathrm{ord}}_P)_P}\bigoplus_{P\in C}\mathbb Z/\ell\right)
 \simeq\mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}(C)[\ell].$$ Its dimension over $\mathbb F_\ell$ is $2g(C)$. The kernel of all exact point orders on $\widehat E$ is the Tate module $T_\ell\mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}(C)$ and has $\mathbb Z_\ell$-rank $2g(C)$.

The set $\mathcal S$ is infinite. For every $z\in E^\times$, every $j\geq1$, and every representative $g\in L^\times$ of $\Theta[z]\bmod\ell^j$, all but finitely many $D\in\mathcal S$ satisfy $$\label{eq:recovery-residue-powers}
 \operatorname{ord}_D(g)=0,
 \qquad g|_D\in l(D)^{\times\ell^j}.$$

Let $l$ be algebraically closed, let $X/l$ be a normal integral projective variety of dimension $d\geq2$, and let $\mathcal S$ be an infinite set of prime divisors of bounded degree in a fixed projective embedding. Let $\mathcal A$ be any collection of pairs $(g,q)$, where $g\in l(X)^\times$ and $q\geq1$ is prime to $\operatorname{char}l$. Suppose that, for each pair separately, all but finitely many $D\in\mathcal S$ satisfy $$\operatorname{ord}_D(g)=0,
 \qquad g|_D\in l(D)^{\times q}.$$ There exist a finite field extension $M/l(X)$ and a curve field $P_0/l$ contained in $M$ such that $M/P_0$ is regular and $$g\in(M\overline{P_0})^{\times q}
 \quad\text{for every }(g,q)\in\mathcal A.$$ The same fields $M$ and $P_0$ work for the entire collection.
